# Agents Architecture

## Objective

Enable modular, intelligent analysis through specialized agents.

## Agents Overview

### 1. Data Analyst Agent

- Processes raw data
- Identifies patterns

### 2. Financial Analyst Agent

- Interprets financial metrics
- Generates insights

### 3. Risk Agent

- Detects financial risks
- Generates alerts

### 4. Investment Advisor Agent

- Suggests allocation strategies

### 5. Debt Strategy Agent

- Builds debt repayment plans

## Communication Flow

1. Data Analyst -> processes data
2. Financial Analyst -> interprets
3. Risk Agent -> evaluates risks
4. Strategy Agents -> recommend actions

## Implementation Strategy

### Phase 1 (Cursor)

- Use `.mdc` files as agent definitions
- Manual orchestration via prompts

### Phase 2 (Backend)

- Convert agents into services
- Use jobs and queues
- Automate execution

## Rules

- Each agent must have a single responsibility
- Avoid overlapping logic
- Keep agents modular

## Future

- Autonomous agents
- AI integration
- Real-time decision engines
